    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30643" root="عن" body-key="E">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعَنَّ</span></b>  [<i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَعَرَّضَ</span>]. One says, ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْنَنْتُ بِعُنَّةٍ</span></b> 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا أَدْرِى مَا هِىَ</span>, (S, K, but in the latter <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لا ادرى</span>,)
meaning <i>I addressed, applied,</i> or <i>directed, myself
to a thing</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَعَرَّضْتُ لِشَىْءٍ</span>) <i>not knowing what it
was.</i> (S, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْنَنْتُهُ لِكَذَا</span> <i>I exposed him,</i>
or <i>caused him to become exposed,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَرَّضْتُهُ</span>,) <i>to such
a thing;</i> and <i>I turned him to it,</i> or <i>towards it.</i>
(S.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْننْتُ اللِّجَامَ</span> <i>I put a rein</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِنَان</span>) <i>to the
bit;</i> (S, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَنَّنْتُهُ</span></b> , (S, * K,) inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَعْنِينٌ</span>; (S;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَنَنْتُهُ</span></b> . (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See also 1,
last quarter, in three places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُعِنَّ عَنِ ٱمْرَأَتِهِ</span>:
see 2.

